<title>GERMANY: Toepfer pegs 1997 EU grain crop at 196-199 mln T.</title>
<headline>Toepfer pegs 1997 EU grain crop at 196-199 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain trader Alfred C Toepfer's monthly market report for July put the likely 1997 European Union grain crop at 196-199 million tonnes, against a June forecast for 197-200 million.</p>
<p>Last year's crop was put at 200 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Toepfer said early harvest results in the Mediterranean and northern France were the reason for the cut in the range.  </p>
<p>But crops in northern Europe were in good shape.</p>
<p>Toepfer gave the following breakdown for 1997 -- soft wheat 89 million tonnes (91 million 1996), durum wheat six million (7.5), barley 51 (52) and maize broadly unchanged at 32.5 million.</p>
<p>Triticale was put at 4.5 million tonnes, up 600,0000.</p>
<p>Toepfer did not offer specific forecasts for rye, oats, sorghum or other grains.</p>
<p>The EU Commission said last week it expected at crop of 200 million tonnes against its own estimate of a record 201.5 million last year.</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
